This includes your cleaning tools and your cleaning supplies. I've been using the Dyson Pencil Vac. I love that the LED light makes all of that dust super visible and the charging dock makes everything really accessible so there's no excuse not to vacuum. I also keep my bathroom cleaner out and my kitchen cleaner because when everything is out of sight, it's out of mind and I'm much less likely to clean. Create special stations or zones. This one has been a game changer. So whether it's a tea and coffee station or a cleaning station or even a pet food station, you'll spend less time looking for everything. To get rid of that chronic clutter that affects so many people with ADHD, keep trash cans in almost every room. Don't fold what doesn't need folding. No one has to know. Organize around your actual habits. So if you leave your keys by your coffee station, just put a tray there. You don't have to overthink it.", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "List"}, {"shortCode": "DbnwjwCSl-H", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbnwjwCSl-H/", "caption": "#ad How to wash a dirty kitchen sink featuring the NEW Punch Sponge by @ocedarclean #PunchSponge #kitchensink #OCedar #PunchHitsDifferent", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T14:19:13.000Z", "videoDuration": 42.166, "videoPlayCount": 2591, "videoViewCount": 1081, "likesCount": 52, "commentsCount": 2, "displayUrl": "https://instagram.fhnd4-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t51.71878-15/767068614_4440874772819010_5530642787662547184_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e15_tt6&_nc_ht=instagram.fhnd4-1.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=Q6cZ2gHP-7CF3hMglWo6UQZ1KgzRRrL3kaP_ZF8pM8ZaV-dHHScuErnTxIL3e2LVLcgM4PK5x-kF_G7Xwr4jBN1hd4fY&_nc_ohc=3Dz5MfWQsFcQ7kNvwF2LPAu&_nc_gid=M51aDDXKYvFxPeJgYkIOAw&edm=ADp7STQBAAAA&ccb=7-5&oh=00_AQFfFQ3TYyMw7JnL2C0Wv7bN8W-XQWt8i-0C2Mkh6IWH2g&oe=6A877C0E&_nc_sid=c6f216", "videoUrl": "https://instagram.fhnd4-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m86/AQN9dbMSpDutSerhQmv5ohnANSM_WwITKL4UeYxOeiUKpnp5B5KOBnl66zN2MO3jkFPv70XZto19PJ1KL5WZ2k3Znp9eXi3ghxFpbXc.mp4?_nc_ca