5, "likes": 93, "comments": 2}, {"date": "2026-08-16", "plays": 3052, "likes": 94, "comments": 2}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "Here are five realistic cleaning habits to keep your home tidy. This says Sweetie contemplates the meaning of life. Handle the mail right away. I know, I know, everyone's favorite habit. Toss junk mail in a nearby wastebasket and important mail goes at my desk. Make your bed every day. It doesn't have to look perfect, it just has to get done. Because there's nothing better than getting into a made bed. Wipe surfaces every day, especially your bathroom sink to keep the toothpaste gunk at bay. This all-purpose cleaner is so pretty I can just keep it out. And when I say surfaces, I also mean kitchen counters. My grandmother always said never go to bed with dirty kitchen counters. Okay, she didn't say that, but someone's grandmother definitely did. So simple yet effective, do a nightly five-minute reset. That means hanging up everyone's favorite floor clothes. You can hang them on hooks if they're not yet ready to go in the wash, and they're also not yet ready to be hung back up. Put any bags away, put any cats away. This blanket is Sweetie's kryptonite. Wash and put away dishes from some Rice Krispie treats I made earlier. I use automatic dish soap to make washing pots and pans a lot easier. There's something about a dish-free sink that makes life feel better. And speaking of feeling better, don't forget to treat yourself every single day.", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "List"}, {"shortCode": "DbTxQDqhd4W", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbTxQDqhd4W/", "caption": "How to keep your cat happy with @temptationscats #cats #home #cat #cats_of_instagram \ud83d\ude3b", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T20:00:28.000Z", "videoDuration": 66.2, "videoPlayCount": 3123, "videoViewCount": 500, "likesCount": 89, "commentsCount": 2, "displayUrl": "https://scontent-cdg4-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/759329297_18121786045828197_1486465856699009